    "command": "# Check the round-trip issue: formToYaml uses sys_execve, yamlToForm also handles sys_execve
# But formToYaml collapses all process rules into ONE kprobe with ALL binaries as values.
# yamlToForm then expands them back into one ProcessRule per binary.
# The net effect: input [{binaries:["a"]}, {binaries:["b"]}] -> output [{binaries:["a"]}, {binaries:["b"]}]
# That seems fine. But what about [{binaries:["a","b"]}]? formToYaml flatMaps binaries.
# allBinaries = ["a","b"]. yamlToForm creates [{binaries:["a"]},{binaries:["b"]}].
# So multi-binary ProcessRule is split. Check PolicyForm's handling of processBinaries.
grep -n "processBinaries\\|map.*binaries\\[0\\]" /home/bigred/Sentinel/web/src/components/PolicyForm/PolicyForm.tsx",
