  "tool_input": {
    "command": "# parsedFromMatchArgs = true is inside the outer for-ma loop, line 53
# So if matchArgsIdx0 has elements, flag gets set; if empty, stays false. Correct.

# Check: debounce saveToStorage — on unmount, cleanup fires clearTimeout, but saveToStorage
# is NOT called on unmount. The pending write is cancelled, so events are LOST if component
# unmounts while timer is pending. This is the memory-safe path (no leak), but it means
# if the window is closed or component unmounts (e.g. hot reload), the last N events
# within the 2s debounce window won't be persisted.
# Is this a correctness bug? Debatable — it's a UX/data-loss issue, not a crash.

# Check builder.go: the network kprobe is only generated if len(netAddresses) > 0
# What if someone sets networkMode=whitelist, leaves addresses empty, adds ports?
# → No kprobe is generated at all → ports are silently ignored
# Same in formToYaml.ts: netAddresses.length > 0 guard at line 75

# Check: builder.go DPort index vs NetAddr index — both use Index: 0 with "sock" type
# Tetragon DPort/DAddr selectors on tcp_connect use index 0 which is the sock argument
# This is correct per Tetragon docs.

# Check EMPTY_FORM has namespace: 'default' hardcoded
# When user opens New Policy, form pre-selects 'default' namespace
# If user wants cluster-wide, they must manually change it — but this isn't a bug per se

# Check handleTabChange lines 86-90: setPolicyMode wrapped in "if (parsed.namespace !== undefined)"
# This is definitely a bug: cluster-wide policies (namespace=undefined) will never update policyMode
# when switching from YAML back to Form tab
echo "analysis done"",
    "description": "Final analysis of remaining candidates"
  }
}

