// Check: dedup only checks prev[0] - the MOST RECENT event.
// If same event arrives but another event was interspersed, dedup misses it.
// This is a design limitation, not necessarily a bug.

// More important: MAX_EVENTS truncation combined with dedup:
// Line 90: return [{...evt, count:1, severity}, ...prev].slice(0, MAX_EVENTS)
// When array is exactly 500 and a NON-duplicate arrives, the OLDEST event is dropped - correct.
// When a DUPLICATE of prev[0] arrives: line 88-89: [...prev[0] updated, ...prev.slice(1)]
// prev.slice(1) is 499 elements, so total stays at 500 (if was 500). Correct.
// No truncation bug here.

// Check: isSameEvent uses a.time (DisplayEvent.time) vs b.time (TetragonEvent.time)
// For dedup: a.time was UPDATED to evt.time on each dedup merge (line 88: time: evt.time)
// So the 5s window is relative to the LAST seen duplicate, not the first. Correct sliding window.
console.log('dedup logic looks correct')
"
",
    "description": "Verify dedup and MAX_EVENTS logic correctness"
  }
}

