{
  "event": "PreToolUse",
  "tool_name": "Bash",
  "tool_input": {
    "command": "node -e "
// Check the localLabels useEffect dependency in PolicyForm.tsx (line 52-58):
// The effect depends on a computed JSON.stringify(sorted podSelector).
// This is called with: JSON.stringify(Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(value.podSelector ?? {}).sort(...)))
// This is constructed inline in the dep array.
// Problem: On every render, this creates a NEW string object, but since React does shallow
// comparison and strings are compared by value, this is FINE if content is same.
// HOWEVER: the real issue is: this useEffect fires every time 'value' changes (via parent onChange),
// because value.podSelector changes reference on every onChange call from the form itself.
// But the JSON.stringify guard prevents re-firing if content is same - that's working.

// A subtler issue: the dep array contains a complex expression, not just 'value.podSelector'.
// React will call this expression on every render to get the dep value.
// This is inefficient but not a correctness bug.

// Real stale closure issue: In PolicyEditPage.tsx handleTabChange (line 80-92):
// yamlToForm(yamlContent) is called, parsed.namespace is checked,
// then yamlContent.toLowerCase().includes('sigkill') is called on the SAME content.
// This is fine - yamlContent is captured from outer scope, not stale here.
// But: 'action' used in handleTabChange comes from component scope, derived from policyMode.
// policyMode changes DON'T cause handleTabChange to re-register (it uses setActiveTab etc.)
// handleTabChange is recreated on every render since it's defined as a plain function, not useCallback.
// So it's not stale. Fine.

console.log('No stale closure in handleTabChange')
"
",
    "description": "Check stale closure in PolicyEditPage handleTabChange"
  }
}

