// This is a perf issue but not a correctness bug per se.

// More important: check the useEffect that calls connect():
// useEffect(() => { connect(); return () => esRef.current?.close() }, [])
// connect is NOT in the dep array. ESLint would warn. But functionally, since
// connect() only uses stable refs (esRef, setConnected, setError, setEvents),
