{
  "event": "PreToolUse",
  "tool_name": "Bash",
  "tool_input": {
    "command": "node -e "
// Check: SecurityEventsProvider - debounce on unmount
// useEffect returns cleanup that calls clearTimeout only (cancels pending save).
// If the component is unmounted with pending events (tab close, page refresh, navigate away),
// the 2s pending save is cancelled and events are LOST.
// The fix would be to call saveToStorage(events) in the cleanup before clearTimeout,
// but the cleanup doesn't have access to the latest 'events' value since it's a closure.
// Actually it DOES: the cleanup in useEffect([events]) captures the current 'events' via closure.
// So the cleanup CAN call saveToStorage(events) - but currently it doesn't.
// This is a real data loss bug on page unload.

// However: there's ALSO a beforeunload case. If the user closes the TAB entirely,
// the React cleanup MAY not run synchronously. localStorage writes in beforeunload ARE reliable.
// But this app doesn't register a beforeunload handler.

// Summary of bugs found:
// 1. builder.go line 76: ports-only (no addresses) → silent no-op (same bug in formToYaml line 75)
// 2. PolicyEditPage.tsx line 86: policyMode not updated for cluster-wide policies on yaml→form switch
// 3. SecurityEventsProvider.tsx line 112-114: debounce cleanup cancels timer without flushing → events lost on unmount
// 4. The 'reconnect' function recreated on every render causes unnecessary context re-renders (perf, not correctness)
console.log('Summary complete')
"
",
    "description": "Summarize all confirmed bugs"
  }
}

