fix: use /proc/cmdline instead of readlink exe for running process scan

readlink /proc/<pid>/exe from a different mount namespace (Tetragon container)
returns paths with '(deleted)' suffix for container binaries, causing them all
to be filtered out. /proc/<pid>/cmdline (argv[0]) is read from kernel memory
and is mount-namespace-independent, so it always returns the actual binary path.

Also added stderr capture and per-node found-count logging to aid diagnosis.

