Tetragon's Postfix is a suffix match. When a binary is executed with a
relative path (e.g. execve("cgichild.sh",...) instead of "/cgichild.sh"),
the string "cgichild.sh" does not end with "/cgichild.sh", causing the
NotPostfix allowlist to fire incorrectly and kill the process.

