feat: add File Access Rules (LSM) using lsmhooks: file_open

Uses Tetragon's lsmhooks with file_open hook to block file access at open
time, before any data is read or written. More reliable than
security_file_permission + Sigkill for preventing reads because the block
happens before the VFS layer reads data.

Generated YAML:
  lsmhooks:
    - hook: "file_open"
      args: [{index: 0, type: "file"}]
      selectors:
        - matchArgs: [{index: 0, operator: Prefix, values: [/etc/passwd]}]
          matchActions: [{action: Sigkill}]

Supports Exceptions (matchBinaries: NotIn) per rule.
Existing File Rules (security_file_permission) unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
EOF
